// Open product questions, answered in the running app:
//
//     cargo run -- --review            (this file; answers -> answers.ron)
//
// Schema: `gradiance_scene::review` (QuestionSet). Process: docs/orchestration.md,
// "Review mode". Option paths are relative to this file. Prefer `.scm` scenes:
// a `.ron` scene is rejected by the next FORMAT_VERSION bump, a script is not.
// Each option's scripts run in order, one frame apart, so a later script can
// index (`body-index-at`) what an earlier one spawned.
//
// Only **interactive** questions belong here (owner, 2026-11-17): a choice the
// owner judges in a live scene. A plan decision is made by the session and
// recorded in archive.ron as a `decision: true` entry; it is not asked.
(
    version: 1,
    questions: [
        (
            id: "fluid-look",
            title: "How should water look?",
            source: "Q-5 (#305 screenshots): the owner found the water inherits the solid-body look",
            description: r#"Fluid regions (a pool, a tank, a sea) were drawn like any body: toon bands, the bevelled relief and the outline, made translucent. That reads as a glass block rather than water. These options draw water in its own way. Every option keeps the light surface line along the top.

Settings are global, so flip between the options rather than viewing them side by side. Press play: the box, the ball and the plank float half under; the heavy ball in the right tank sinks through. Judge how the water reads against the bodies in it and behind it, and whether the submerged parts show. Orbit (middle-drag) to see the sides of the pool. A fifth look, `Outline` (a faint tint that keeps the outline), is in Settings > Render if none of these fits."#,
            options: [
                (
                    label: "Shaded body (today)",
                    caption: "The body's toon bands, relief and outline at 45 % opacity.",
                    scripts: ["scenes/fluid-look/scene.scm", "scenes/fluid-look/water.scm"],
                ),
                (
                    label: "Flat tint",
                    caption: "An even, unlit tint of the fill at 45 %; no bands, relief or outline.",
                    scripts: ["scenes/fluid-look/scene.scm", "scenes/fluid-look/water.scm"],
                    settings: (render: (fluid_look: Flat)),
                ),
                (
                    label: "Clear",
                    caption: "A light, mostly see-through tint (22 %); no outline.",
                    scripts: ["scenes/fluid-look/scene.scm", "scenes/fluid-look/water.scm"],
                    settings: (render: (fluid_look: Clear)),
                ),
                (
                    label: "Deep",
                    caption: "A darker tint toward deep blue at 68 %; hides more of what is under it.",
                    scripts: ["scenes/fluid-look/scene.scm", "scenes/fluid-look/water.scm"],
                    settings: (render: (fluid_look: Deep)),
                ),
            ],
        ),
    ],
)
